*.py[cod]
.DS_Store
.caller-review-prompt.md
# The fkst-monitor operational tool is a load-bearing repo artifact (SKILL.md + scripts + tests),
# tracked from before `.claude/` was ignored. A blanket `.claude/` made the rule lie about reality:
# tracked files stayed tracked, but every NEW file of that tool was rejected, so adding a test to it
# required `git add -f` — routing around the rule until the rule means nothing.
# Excluding directory CONTENTS (`dir/*`) rather than the directory itself (`dir/`) is what makes the
# re-include possible at all: git does not descend into an excluded directory, so a `!` under a
# `.claude/` rule can never be evaluated. Each level is therefore opened one step at a time.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
.claude/skills/*
!.claude/skills/fkst-monitor/
.echo-review.md
.fkst/env
.fkst/run/
.sshx-*
/.lake/
/Papers/build/
/build/
__pycache__/
